190
00:10:13.181 --> 00:10:16.082
Count-Min sketch: d rows of w counters.

191
00:10:16.362 --> 00:10:21.482
Each event increments one counter per row, and the estimate is the minimum across rows.

192
00:10:21.762 --> 00:10:32.471
It only over-estimates, by at most εN with probability 1minus δ, for w = e or ε and d = ln(1 or δ).

193
00:10:32.751 --> 00:10:34.799
Pair it with a heap to track candidates.

194
00:10:35.079 --> 00:10:39.453
It merges by adding counters, so partitions and time buckets combine.

195
00:10:39.733 --> 00:10:41.674
Space-Saving or Misra, Gries:

196
00:10:43.024 --> 00:10:44.091
k counters.

197
00:10:44.371 --> 00:10:48.104
A new key replaces the smallest counter and inherits its count.

198
00:10:48.384 --> 00:10:53.824
It guarantees any item with frequency N or k is present, with error at most N or k.

199
00:10:54.104 --> 00:11:00.419
Here N or k = 20,000, larger than item 100's count, so the guarantee is loose.

200
00:11:00.699 --> 00:11:03.301
On a skewed stream the real error was zero.

201
00:11:03.581 --> 00:11:09.277
Sampling is cheap and surprisingly good for the head of the distribution, but noisy near the cut-off.

202
00:11:09.557 --> 00:11:12.139
It is fine for dashboards and not for billing.

203
00:11:13.489 --> 00:11:20.315
Sliding windows: keep sketches per small bucket (for example, 1 minute), and merge the last 60 for an hour.

204
00:11:20.595 --> 00:11:22.281
