239
00:12:28.176 --> 00:12:30.075
Local top-K lists don't merge.

240
00:12:30.355 --> 00:12:38.141
An item can be high in every partition without being top in any, and partitions that didn't list it contribute zero to its count.

241
00:12:38.421 --> 00:12:42.304
Asking for more (c, K) often works but carries no guarantee.

242
00:12:42.584 --> 00:12:43.843
TPUT is exact:

243
00:12:44.123 --> 00:12:48.069
Collect local top-K lists and use them to set a lower bound τ.

244
00:12:48.349 --> 00:12:52.509
Fetch every item with a local count ≥ τ or m.

245
00:12:52.789 --> 00:12:54.645
Get exact counts for the survivors.

246
00:12:55.995 --> 00:12:59.686
Partition by the ranking key (shuffle by SKU) when you can.

247
00:12:59.966 --> 00:13:07.113
Then each SKU is counted in one place, and the global top-K is a merge of disjoint local top-Ks.

248
00:13:07.393 --> 00:13:08.715
That merge is exact.

249
00:13:08.995 --> 00:13:13.411
Sketches that add (Count-Min, HLL) merge exactly by construction.

250
00:13:13.691 --> 00:13:17.126
This is one reason to prefer them for distributed pipelines.

