496
00:29:49.077 --> 00:30:06.207
M4) shuffle all counts by product (exact) 10 or 10 0 or 10 1,509,929. then an item that is, say, 12 in every city can be near the top nationally, yet. appears in nobody's local top-10.

497
00:30:06.487 --> 00:30:13.463
Merging local top lists misses such items (4 of the true 10 here) and. under-counts the ones it does report.

498
00:30:13.743 --> 00:30:15.258
The rest is in the chapter.

499
00:30:18.108 --> 00:30:18.961
Reading it:

500
00:30:19.241 --> 00:30:24.340
Merging local top-10s misses 4 of the true top-10 and gets half the counts wrong.

501
00:30:24.620 --> 00:30:28.353
Local top-100s happened to work here, with no guarantee.

502
00:30:28.633 --> 00:30:35.268
TPUT is exact at 4,950 pairs, about 300x less than shuffling everything.

503
00:30:35.548 --> 00:30:39.047
In production, key by SKU so the problem disappears.

504
00:30:39.327 --> 00:30:40.777
Use TPUT where you can't.

